# HSBG writes these at runtime. None of them belong in the repository.

# The diagnostic log, which has never been tracked and should stay that way.
# The script writes a fresh one beside itself on every machine that runs it, so
# a committed copy would only be one stale session — and since every line in it
# carries an absolute path, it would carry a Windows username with it.
# Listed here so a stray `git add -A` from a folder you have been testing in
# cannot sweep it in.
HSBG.log
HSBG.log.1

# Downloaded by the update check, beside the script, named for its version.
HSBG Script Final v*.ahk

# The settings file is deliberately NOT ignored: the copy in this repository is
# the documented default, and the script regenerates an identical one if it is
# missing. If you keep personal settings here, ignore it locally instead
# (git update-index --skip-worktree "HSBG Config.ini") rather than committing
# your own paths.
